  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1230 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions look to continue through the upcoming work \nweek as an upper-level ridge will remain over the Desert Southwest \nand west Texas.  This ridge should expand slightly with 500mb \nheights at 594dam and 850mb temperatures of 23 to 26 deg C. \nSoutherly winds and mostly sunny skies should prevail.  As a result, \nhigh temperatures should range from the upper 90s to the low 100s \nduring this time.  The warmest conditions are most likely to occur \nacross the Big Country from Wednesday onward where the highest mid-\nlevel heights will be located and could reach heat advisory\ncriteria.",
